@Identity_HostAddress = https://localhost:7102

### 1. Register -> expect 201 Created + Location header
POST {{Identity_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "uday@commerceflow.local",
  "password": "Str0ngPass",
  "fullName": "Uday L"
}

### 2. Same email again -> expect 409 Conflict
POST {{Identity_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "uday@commerceflow.local",
  "password": "Str0ngPass",
  "fullName": "Duplicate"
}

### 3. Weak password -> expect 400 with an "errors" array from Identity's validators
POST {{Identity_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "weak@commerceflow.local",
  "password": "alllowercase",
  "fullName": "Weak Password"
}

### 4. Login -> expect 200 with accessToken + refreshToken
POST {{Identity_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "uday@commerceflow.local",
  "password": "Str0ngPass"
}

### 5. Wrong password -> expect 401. Compare with #6: the responses are identical.
POST {{Identity_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "uday@commerceflow.local",
  "password": "WrongPass1"
}

### 6. Unknown email -> expect the SAME 401, so nobody can enumerate accounts
POST {{Identity_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@commerceflow.local",
  "password": "WrongPass1"
}

@accessToken = PASTE-ACCESS-TOKEN-HERE
@refreshToken = PASTE-REFRESH-TOKEN-HERE
@userId = PASTE-USER-ID-HERE

### 7. Who am I -> expect 200
GET {{Identity_HostAddress}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 8. No token -> expect 401
GET {{Identity_HostAddress}}/api/users/me

### 9. Admin-only endpoint as a Customer -> expect 403 (not 401!)
GET {{Identity_HostAddress}}/api/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 10. Refresh -> expect 200 with a DIFFERENT refresh token
POST {{Identity_HostAddress}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### 11. Send the OLD refresh token again -> expect 401, and every session is revoked
POST {{Identity_HostAddress}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### 12. Log in as the seeded administrator
POST {{Identity_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@commerceflow.local",
  "password": "Admin#12345"
}

### 13. Logout -> expect 204 (and 204 again for an unknown token)
POST {{Identity_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}
